tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commits/db0b6f140b46605d84f6dc8cec946a5918986ee8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:12:47Z","email":"chrisdev92@outlook.com","name":"ChristianCL92"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T17:34:53Z","email":"chrisdev92@outlook.com","name":"ChristianCL92"},"message":"point the root readme down at the sub docs instead of above the repo\n\nLine 5 read \"See ../../README.md for full project context\". Two levels up\nfrom the repository root is outside the project, so the link had no valid\ntarget. It is the correct path from programs/rental_escrow/README.md, which\ncarries the same sentence at its line 7, so it arrived here by being copied\nfrom a file two directories deeper.\n\nAt the root the sentence cannot be repaired by fixing the path, because this\nfile is the full project context and there is nothing above it to point at.\nIt now points down at the two sub readmes instead. The Documentation section\nalready lists both, but that sits near the bottom, and a reader landing on a\nmonorepo root wants to know at the top that the two exist.","tree":{"sha":"509507a2acde13618da5442d25e8484800a4a509","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/git/trees/509507a2acde13618da5442d25e8484800a4a509"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/git/commits/db0b6f140b46605d84f6dc8cec946a5918986ee8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119958000?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92","id":119958000,"login":"ChristianCL92","node_id":"U_kgDOByZp8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commit/db0b6f140b46605d84f6dc8cec946a5918986ee8","node_id":"C_kwDOQXYdJNoAKGRiMGI2ZjE0MGI0NjYwNWQ4NGY2ZGM4Y2VjOTQ2YTU5MTg5ODZlZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commit/b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d","sha":"b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commits/b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d"}],"sha":"db0b6f140b46605d84f6dc8cec946a5918986ee8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commits/db0b6f140b46605d84f6dc8cec946a5918986ee8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119958000?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92","id":119958000,"login":"ChristianCL92","node_id":"U_kgDOByZp8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commits/b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:21:54Z","email":"chrisdev92@outlook.com","name":"ChristianCL92"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T17:34:53Z","email":"chrisdev92@outlook.com","name":"ChristianCL92"},"message":"document the marketing copy generator and link it from the footer\n\nThe tool was reachable only by reading the source, so neither of the two\naudiences could find it: someone reading the repo on GitHub had nothing to\nread, and someone on the live site had nothing to click.\n\nThe footer link fixes the second. It sits with the Instagram and WhatsApp\nicons because those are the two channels the tool writes for, so it reads as\npart of the set rather than something bolted on.\n\nThe root README gains a feature bullet, the tools/ and api/marketing entries\nin the project structure, and a section covering what the tool does, why the\nendpoint is public, and the three bounds that make that acceptable: 4 requests\nan hour per ip, a 1000 token cap, and the provider spend cap. The demo section\nnow leads with it, since it is the only feature that needs no wallet, no\ndevnet USDC and no sign-in, and troubleshooting explains that the hourly limit\nis the limiter working rather than a broken page.\n\nTwo gaps that predate this feature are closed while here: UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL\nand _TOKEN were never in the environment table despite rate limiting already\nbeing in use, and the frontend README still claimed frontend tests could be\nadded one day, which stopped being true when test:unit started running.\n\nThe architecture diagram is deliberately untouched. Its right hand column\ndescends into Supabase, so listing marketing copy there would have claimed a\nwrite path that does not exist, which is the opposite of what the feature\ndoes. The generator gets its own diagram in its own section instead.","tree":{"sha":"8d14e03eea3c2345dca0a419234125474c2ef8ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/git/trees/8d14e03eea3c2345dca0a419234125474c2ef8ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/git/commits/b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119958000?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92","id":119958000,"login":"ChristianCL92","node_id":"U_kgDOByZp8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChristianCL92","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/commit/b542cbe689102e89d839d92556db8bb11104fb0d","node_id":"C_kwDOQXYdJNoAKGI1NDJjYmU2ODkxMDJlODlkODM5ZDkyNTU2ZGI4YmIxMTEwNGZiMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ChristianCL92/rental_escrow/com