at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22563792?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503","id":22563792,"login":"scottyj503","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTYzNzky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottyj503","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/f8de13134306ca3ca81b3797608a627c1dd3f19a","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKGY4ZGUxMzEzNDMwNmNhM2NhODFiMzc5NzYwOGE2MjdjMWRkM2YxOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d","sha":"9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d"}],"sha":"f8de13134306ca3ca81b3797608a627c1dd3f19a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/f8de13134306ca3ca81b3797608a627c1dd3f19a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:35:26Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:35:26Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: inspect network payload for submit/mutation fixes (Phase 2.5)\n\nLesson from PARTS-954 (2026-05-12, PARTS-961-BB bug-bash): a fix that\nremoved UI validation errors silently traded them for a malformed API\npayload. The empty default line item was skipped in\nvalidateForSubmission/validateForDraft but still lived in data.lineItems\nat submit time, so transformFormDataToInput mapped over it and\ncreatePurchaseOrders fired with vendorId: \"\" and a blank partNumber.\nThe after-screenshot showed \"no validation errors, no aria-invalid\ninputs\" — marked PASS — but the network request told a different story.\nCaught only on code review.\n\nPhase 2.5 now requires explicit network-payload inspection for any fix\ntouching submit / validation / network-triggering paths:\n\n- Before submit: snapshot outstanding requests via\n  mcp__playwright__browser_network_requests\n- Click submit (or trigger the action)\n- List requests again; identify the new one (or confirm none was made\n  if validation should have blocked)\n- Assert four things on the new request:\n  - Was it made at all?\n  - Is the URL correct?\n  - Is the payload well-formed (required fields populated, no\n    placeholder rows leaking, types match schema)?\n  - Did the response succeed (200/204 vs swallowed 4xx)?\n- Document the network-level result in the after-fix runtime-check\n  section of the report + PR description.\n\nNet rule: a green test suite + a passing UI check + an unverified\nnetwork payload is STILL not a complete fix for submission-shaped bugs.\n\nReflects the feedback-form-submit-network-verify and (existing in\nspirit) feedback-live-verify-both-phases memories from the\nPARTS-961-BB session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da40fa48215c2e58a54bb6f0f177bebb81218f70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/da40fa48215c2e58a54bb6f0f177bebb81218f70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDliZTY3OWE0NTEyZDNmZjYzYjIzOTcwMmQ2ZTkwYWM1MWIyNWNkMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46","sha":"78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46"}],"sha":"9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/9be679a4512d3ff63b239702d6e90ac51b25cd1d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:32:49Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:32:49Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: drop the cross-reference table (not load-bearing)\n\nThe \"Memory references\" table at the bottom was misleading: the\nagent doesn''t actually know where the memory files live at runtime\n(paths depend on slugified CWD which varies per worktree), and the\ncontent is already baked into the prompt for PARTS. The table only\nserved maintainer use (\"where do I edit to update the rule?\") and\neven that was thin since cross-references within the prompt are\nself-referential (\"see Fullbay PARTS context above\", \"baked into\nOperating constraint #4\").\n\n- Removed the 10-row \"Memory references\" table entirely.\n- Replaced with a compact \"Running against a non-PARTS project\"\n  section that captures the actually-load-bearing fallback rule:\n  read CWD memory first, then repo CLAUDE.md, then ask the user.\n  Never substitute PARTS values for another project. Confirm\n  transition IDs via /transitions endpoint in unfamiliar projects.\n- 22 lines removed, 9 added. Prompt is tighter and less misleading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6fb5a24c02a5d69529fbef250cff9c81b504760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/d6fb5a24c02a5d69529fbef250cff9c81b504760"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDc4YmMwNGI2N2Y0OGI1ZjRhOThlNjk0ODUxNTdjMGZiOWM0NGVhNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4","sha":"3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4"}],"sha":"78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/78bc04b67f48b5f4a98e69485157c0fb9c44ea46"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:20:18Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:20:18Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: surface fan-out opportunities in remaining I/O-heavy steps\n\nOperating constraint #2 says \"fan out by default\" but several\nI/O-heavy or per-ticket steps still read as serial loops. Made the\nparallelism explicit at four more points where independent work was\nsitting on a single sequential `for` loop:\n\n- Phase 0.4 (claim writes): per-ticket field PUTs and transition POSTs\n  are independent pure I/O — fire all N in parallel, same for the\n  verification GETs.\n- Phase 1.1 (fetch full tickets): N independent Jira REST fetches —\n  fire in parallel (Bash-per-ticket in one message, or one subagent\n  per ticket when also downloading attachments).\n- Phase 1.6 (apply verdict mutations): same pattern as 0.4 — comment\n  POSTs and any Closed transitions fan out across tickets.\n- Phase 2.8 (batched parallel fixing): clarified the fan-out applies\n  at three layers — worktree setup per ticket, TDD red/green per\n  ticket AND per file, synthesis always in the top-level agent.\n- Phase 2.9 (FF PR review feedback): note that when an FF spans\n  multiple reviewer comments / files, the same per-file fan-out\n  discipline from Phase 2.2–2.4 applies.\n\nNet effect: every step where parallel subagents would help now says\nso. Steps that are inherently single-threaded (Phase 2.5 runtime\ngreen-check, Phase 2.6 verification bundle, Phase 3 wrap) still have\ntheir explicit \"don''t fan out\" callouts unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54bfb57c888ad38ef3ae6f4449185a07edc40292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/54bfb57c888ad38ef3ae6f4449185a07edc40292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDNiYTc0YmJhNTIzZDhjMTdmM2U0ZTYwMzE4N2ExODllMGYzNjZlYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c","sha":"c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c"}],"sha":"3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/3ba74bba523d8c17f3e4e603187a189e0f366eb4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:18:05Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:18:05Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: anchor shell commands to absolute paths via BUG_BASH_ROOT\n\nRelative paths (`find .`, `cd $REPO`, `../$TICKET/$repo`) break when\nshells change cwd between tool calls or when subagents inherit a\ndifferent working directory. Anchoring everything to one absolute\nbase captured at Phase 0.1 removes the entire class of \"wrong cwd\"\nbugs.\n\n- Phase 0.1: capture BUG_BASH_ROOT=\"$(pwd)\" once. `find` now emits\n  absolute paths via `find \"$BUG_BASH_ROOT\"`. Added explicit\n  convention statement: throughout the prompt, `$BUG_BASH_ROOT` is\n  the parent folder, `$BUG_BASH_ROOT/<repo>` is an absolute repo\n  path, `$BUG_BASH_ROOT/<TICKET>/<repo>` is an absolute worktree\n  path. No `.`, `./`, or `../` in commands.\n- Phase 0.5 (dev server): REPO=<name>, REPO_DIR=\"$BUG_BASH_ROOT/$REPO\";\n  `cd \"$REPO_DIR\"` instead of `cd $REPO`. Branch check via\n  `git -C \"$REPO_DIR\" branch --show-current`.\n- Phase 2.1 (worktree setup): SOURCE_REPO=\"$BUG_BASH_ROOT/$repo\",\n  WORKTREE_DIR=\"$BUG_BASH_ROOT/$TICKET/$repo\". Worktree creation,\n  env-file copy, install/build, and auth-file copy all use absolute\n  paths. Eliminates the `git -C \"$repo\" worktree add \"../$TICKET/$repo\"`\n  shape which relied on cwd being the parent folder.\n- Forge reference expanded with concrete \"when and how to use\" hints:\n  reading FB component source, grepping the emitted CSS bundle (with\n  the escaped-form gotcha), checking Forge''s own CLAUDE.md /\n  Storybook, mirroring test mocks from canonical sources. Absolute\n  path `/Users/scottjones/code/ui-forge-web` re-emphasized.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01fd5f437ceb7ba531f0aee95d85d95c214347cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/01fd5f437ceb7ba531f0aee95d85d95c214347cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKGM4ZWZjZTI3ZjU5MDJlOTliNjBmM2RlM2JjZDk4Y2QyMjUyNmJlOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b","sha":"b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b"}],"sha":"c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/c8efce27f5902e99b60f3de3bcd98cd22526be8c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:14:10Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T23:14:10Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"v6.1: real-world hardening + memory-portability inlining\n\nTwo related sets of changes, shipped together because both make the\nagent more self-contained:\n\nREAL-WORLD HARDENING (six additions captured in README v6.1 bullet):\n\n- Slack MCP tool added to agent''s tools list\n  (mcp__plugin_slack_slack__slack_send_message). Closes the v6.0 gap\n  where Phase 2.7 told the agent to post but didn''t grant the tool.\n- New Section 1.7 \"Refinement and correction addenda\" — canonical\n  shapes for \"Follow-up from live verification (YYYY-MM-DD):\" and\n  \"Correction to the YYYY-MM-DD follow-up:\" comments. Earlier\n  verdicts are never edited; later evidence lands as a new comment.\n- Phase 2.1 worktree warmup added: copy .env / .env.local.test,\n  refresh_codeartifact_token, pnpm i --frozen-lockfile, pnpm run\n  build. The prtins / cenvv-rca-pci-prb alias equivalent. Without\n  this, pre-commit hook''s test:int fails and the agent is tempted\n  to --no-verify.\n- Phase 2.5 hardened — runtime green-check is mandatory before 2.6,\n  even when unit + int tests pass. Pair with /tmp/<TICKET>-after-fix-\n  <timestamp>.png alongside the Phase 1 before-screenshot.\n- Phase 2.7 expanded with a Jira verification comment after PR opens\n  and Slack post — closes the audit trail on the Jira side\n  (four anchors: date, what was verified live, screenshot path,\n  PR link).\n- Phase 2.8 port :8090 contention guidance for parallel commits\n  (serialize / stagger / port override). Explicit \"do NOT default\n  to --no-verify\".\n\nMEMORY-PORTABILITY INLINING (so the agent works in a fresh worktree\nwith no memory):\n\n- New top-level \"Fullbay PARTS context — baked-in defaults\" section\n  with all PARTS knobs: Scott''s accountId, repo names, Forge path,\n  dev port 8090, Jira custom field IDs (10177/10178/10179),\n  transition table (3=Closed, 7=In Dev, etc.), auth header pattern,\n  Slack channel id + format + custom emoji, project conventions\n  (no Tailwind, layout-fix computed-style rule, Forge form quirks),\n  warmup recipe, verification bundle.\n- Operating constraint #3 reframed: baked-in defaults first; memory\n  is an overlay, never block on its absence.\n- Phase 0.2 reframed as \"best-effort overlay\" — agent has defaults\n  baked in; memory provides session-specific overrides or\n  newer-than-baked-in updates.\n- In-text feedback-X / reference-X shorthand replaced with inline\n  guidance where load-bearing. Cross-references kept in a\n  reframed bottom table that explicitly states it''s NOT\n  load-bearing.\n- For non-PARTS projects, the agent still looks up corresponding\n  values from CWD memory or asks the user. Never substitute PARTS\n  values for a non-PARTS project.\n\nNet effect: a fresh /bug-bash run in a new worktree finds no memory,\nproceeds with baked-in PARTS knobs anyway, and only asks the user\nwhen something genuinely can''t be derived. Memory files in\n~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/ remain the canonical\nsource-of-truth for updates over time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a85746adb1deafe91359ea6500fa0cb0783a941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/9a85746adb1deafe91359ea6500fa0cb0783a941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKGIzYWQ2MzQwNjE2YzZiNmM5MzljMTQwZDBmYTQ5OTQxMzJjZDExM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722","sha":"e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722"}],"sha":"b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/b3ad6340616c6b6c939c140d0fa4994132cd113b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:42:59Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:42:59Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: kill dev server on wrap (Phase 3) if we started it\n\nPhase 0.5 launched `pnpm dev` as a backgrounded process but the agent\nnever cleaned it up. A stale Vite server on :8090 between sessions is\nthe documented #1 cause of \"flaky\" Playwright timeouts\n(feedback-check-port-8090-collisions). Leaving one running was a\nfoot-gun for the next bug-bash run.\n\n- Phase 0.5: capture launched PID into /tmp/<repo>-dev.pid only when\n  the agent actually starts the server. If it was already running\n  (lsof returns 0), don''t write the pidfile — we don''t own it.\n- Phase 3 (new step 1, before memory/summary): walk\n  /tmp/*-dev.pid, SIGTERM, sleep, SIGKILL fallback, rm pidfile,\n  verify port free with lsof. Don''t touch processes the agent\n  didn''t start.\n- Final summary now notes whether dev server was killed or left\n  alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6e41fdb1df16686278a3980880f9419ce62c254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/b6e41fdb1df16686278a3980880f9419ce62c254"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKGU5NTA5YTI3MGFjOTlkMWQ3MmExNTc3Yjk2ZTBhM2ZiZGM3OGI3MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e","sha":"76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e"}],"sha":"e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/e9509a270ac99d1d72a1577b96e0a3fbdc78b722"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:40:52Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:40:52Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: claim tickets up front (Phase 0.4) instead of post-verdict\n\nThe team wants WIP signalling when work starts, not when it ends.\nPreviously the agent set Status/Assignee/Dev Owner at Phase 1.6 *after*\nverdicts were approved — by then, anyone else could have grabbed the\nsame ticket while you were verifying. Audit trail also lied: tickets\nwent straight from To Do to In Dev on the same minute the verdict\nlanded, instead of when the work actually started.\n\n- New Phase 0.4 \"Claim the tickets\" — set Status: In Dev (id 7),\n  Assignee: current user, Dev Owner: current user *before* any\n  verification work begins. AskUserQuestion preview on the first\n  ticket, bulk-apply across the rest. Skip tickets already in a\n  non-To-Do state. Verify the batch landed before moving to Phase 1.\n- Renumbered 0.4 (Start dev server) -> 0.5, 0.5 (Inject auth cookies)\n  -> 0.6.\n- Phase 1.5 verdict-to-mutation table reframed: starting state is\n  \"already In Dev / assigned to current user / Dev Owner = current\n  user\" because of the claim. Most verdicts now only need a comment\n  post; only Not-Reproduced triggers a status transition\n  (In Dev -> Closed).\n- Phase 1.6 simplified: drop the bulk Assignee/Dev Owner write\n  (already set at 0.4); just post the comment and run the Closed\n  transition for Not-Reproduced.\n- Cancel-at-checkpoint behavior clarified: the 0.4 claim is NOT\n  reverted — tickets stay In Dev / assigned. Surface that in the\n  cancel summary so the user can manually revert if desired.\n- Fixed stale \"loop back to 1.3\" -> \"loop back to 1.2\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74979807047a6455264c110478b3e50612396dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/74979807047a6455264c110478b3e50612396dc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDc2YzM1YzAzMzk5M2RhNDVkMmRlOWFlZDk3NTNlZTQ0ZmZjNDEwOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41","sha":"68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41"}],"sha":"76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/76c35c033993da45d2de9aed9753ee44ffc4108e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:37:20Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:37:20Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: make MCP repro the baseline verification step\n\nPhase 1.2 used to say source inspection \"often beats UI repro\" for\nwiring/behavior bugs and \"no browser needed\" for code-evidence checks.\nThat downplayed the MCP step — code can lie (dead branches,\nconditional renders, hydration timing) and PR reviewers want\nscreenshots, not greps.\n\n- New lead paragraph: open the running app in MCP and reproduce the\n  reporter''s conditions (route, breakpoint, user state, data) as the\n  baseline for every ticket. Source inspection is a complement.\n- Per-category guidance reframed so MCP is always step one, source\n  inspection layers on top:\n  - Layout/visual: MCP + screenshot is the verification; source\n    confirms layout primitives + computed-style sanity check\n  - Interaction: drive MCP as far as Forge quirks allow; source\n    complements when programmatic input is blocked\n  - State/wiring/behavior: MCP confirms the symptom; source finds\n    the fix site (\"does it manifest?\" vs \"where do we fix it?\")\n  - Code-evidence: still drive MCP first to capture the user-visible\n    symptom for the PR\n- New explicit fallback rule: source-only is acceptable ONLY when\n  the bug condition can''t be reproduced in MCP (prod data, role\n  impersonation, multi-user race). Mark such verdicts explicitly.\n- Capture screenshots during MCP verification -> Evidence section\n  in the report -> PR description.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcd83e5ae8ae72e279764ae953dc7c86ef8b7d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/bcd83e5ae8ae72e279764ae953dc7c86ef8b7d0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDY4ZjY0MWY4OTkzZDIzMDNjZGNiZDQ3OTdmMWE3MjRhODY1NmFlNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada","sha":"60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada"}],"sha":"68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/68f641f8993d2303cdcbd4797f1a724a8656ae41"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T17:58:58Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T17:58:58Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: auth cookie injection + FF PR workflow\n\nTwo patterns surfaced during the 2026-05-12 batch are now baked in:\n\nPhase 0.5 (new) — MCP auth cookie injection recipe per\nreference-mcp-auth-cookies:\n  - Don''t use document.cookie = ... (Descope SDK rejects on\n    http://localhost due to secure:true)\n  - Use page.context().addCookies(...) via\n    mcp__playwright__browser_run_code_unsafe (BrowserContext-level,\n    bypasses page secure-flag enforcement)\n  - Recipe: pnpm test:int:auth -> python3 dump cookies as\n    Playwright-shaped JSON -> paste into browser_run_code_unsafe\n    snippet\n  - MCP harness has no require/fs inside browser_run_code_unsafe,\n    so dump-and-paste is the workable shape\n  - If runtime fails mid-session, tokens expired -> re-run recipe;\n    don''t fall back to document.cookie\n\nPhase 2.9 (new) — review-feedback fork per\nfeedback-fast-follow-pr-workflow:\n  - COMMENTED / CHANGES_REQUESTED -> push to same branch\n    (example: PARTS-945 PR #237, ~20 min to merge)\n  - APPROVED + non-blocking -> Fast-Follow PR\n    (examples: PRs #240, #241 on 2026-05-12)\n  - FF recipe: branch off original PR tip, RED test for fix-shape\n    comments, target original branch -> retarget master after squash\n  - Deleted-base-branch gotcha: gh''s \"Head sha can''t be blank\"\n    error after squash-merge -> rebase onto master + force-with-lease\n  - PR body categorizes comments with Severity + Status (Fixed/\n    Deferred); product-judgement comments deferred by name\n  - Slack: threaded reply with reply_broadcast=true on original PR\n    announcement; canonical Form: \"Fast-follow [PR #N](url)\n    addresses the inline review on this one — <summary> :thank_you:\"\n  - ~30 min typical FF wall-clock\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdb71e3c6d8e6776e4d861a38a67e97edead06b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/bdb71e3c6d8e6776e4d861a38a67e97edead06b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDYwZDc5NDFkMjQxZTc2ODc5OGI1YzY5MTZhYTQyOTg2YWYxMmFhZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0","sha":"2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0"}],"sha":"60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/60d7941d241e768798b5c6916aa42986af12aada"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T17:46:08Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T17:46:08Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: explicit verdict-to-mutation table for Phase 1\n\nThe pause checkpoint and apply-mutations sections implied the\nverdict-to-status mapping in prose, but didn''t spell out exactly\nwhat gets transitioned to what and who becomes assignee + Dev Owner\nper verdict. Easy to drift on.\n\n- Phase 1.5: new verdict-to-mutation table:\n  - Confirmed -> In Dev (id 7), assignee + Dev Owner = current user\n  - Not reproduced -> Closed (id 3), Dev Owner = current user only\n    (assignee unchanged)\n  - Partial/Reframe -> In Dev (id 7), assignee + Dev Owner = current\n    user, comment captures the reframe\n- \"Current user\" defined as JIRA_USER_EMAIL -> accountId, or\n  GET /rest/api/3/myself. Transition IDs read from project memory;\n  PARTS values shown.\n- Checkpoint now has Approve+Phase2, Approve+stop-here, Edit, Cancel\n  (was missing the Cancel option).\n- Phase 1.6: explicit \"bulk-apply, don''t re-prompt per ticket\".\n  JSON example shows the assignee line as omittable for\n  Not-Reproduced. Verification step checks status.name + assignee +\n  Dev Owner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b46914489a21e1b1d04678b74feb0adee1bc3fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/b46914489a21e1b1d04678b74feb0adee1bc3fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDJkM2JkMzZiMTczNDk0NDEwNTUzMTZkNWUwYWVhN2Y5ODVkMDM2YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094","sha":"f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094"}],"sha":"2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/2d3bd36b17349441055316d5e0aea7f985d036a0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:56:23Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:56:23Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: concrete Slack posting spec for Phase 2.7\n\nThe Slack section had the format right but was light on specifics:\nno channel id, no MCP tool reference, no concrete examples, no\nnotes on the Fullbay-custom :thank_you: emoji.\n\n- Channel id (PARTS = C0A4X6JJ2D9) and where to look it up (project\n  memory) for non-PARTS projects\n- Two concrete examples from real PARTS bug-bash PRs (#232, #239)\n- Explicit format rules: PR is a markdown link (not raw URL), repo\n  name in backticks, lowercase summary continuing the \"to <action>\"\n  pattern, custom :thank_you: emoji (not :pray:/:bow:)\n- Use mcp__plugin_slack_slack__slack_send_message with channel id,\n  not the human-readable name\n- One message per PR, no thread\n- Format is canonical -> don''t preview each post, but do report\n  send results to the user\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cf59f551fc0ad63862108cb5a7ab5fa35349532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/0cf59f551fc0ad63862108cb5a7ab5fa35349532"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKGY5Mzg5NmM4NGZhYzU4YTlkMGM0Y2FjYzA2NDhhNjI3ZmFhNzkwOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3","sha":"36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3"}],"sha":"f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/f93896c84fac58a9d0c4cacc0648a627faa79094"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:54:13Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:54:13Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: explicit guidance for fetching ticket attachments\n\nReporter screenshots and screencasts are higher-fidelity repro signal\nthan prose. The previous prompt mentioned ''attachment'' only as a field\nto read, not as something to actually fetch and visually inspect.\n\n- New \"Fetch attachments\" sub-section in 1.1 with curl pattern using\n  attachment.content URL and AUTH_HEADER\n- Per-mimetype handling: images -> Read to view; videos -> extract from\n  filename + prose or surface as an open question at checkpoint;\n  HAR/log -> read as text\n- Inline embedded media in ADF descriptions/comments noted as\n  mediaSingle/media nodes referencing attachment IDs\n- Verified-as-fixed flow now uses reporter screenshots as the source of\n  truth for what \"the original bug\" looked like before claiming repro\n  failure\n\nAlso fixed a stale section reference (1.4 -> 1.5 after the renumbering\nin the prior commit).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d66c608e798b23fe5e2b121787c3244ebb3abb12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/d66c608e798b23fe5e2b121787c3244ebb3abb12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDM2ZTg3NzU1NTJiYzI5N2UzNDI1MzM3NmUzNWE3ZmNhYTZhMmYyYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b","sha":"88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b"}],"sha":"36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/36e8775552bc297e34253376e35a7fcaa6a2f2c3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:53:40Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:53:40Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"bug-bash-runner: fetch full ticket + comments before verifying\n\nThe agent''s Phase 1 said \"fetch the ticket\" without specifying fields or\nthat comments need to be read. Bug-bash triage signal often lives in\ncomments (already-fixed notes, screenshots, narrowed repro conditions),\nso reading the full ticket up front avoids redoing browser work.\n\n- New 1.1 \"Fetch the full ticket\" — explicit field set\n  (summary, description, status, issuetype, priority, assignee, reporter,\n  labels, components, issuelinks, attachment, comment), checklist of key\n  details to review, and common comment patterns to look for\n- Renumbered downstream 1.2-1.6 (verification approach, verdict shape,\n  synthesize, pause, apply mutations)\n- Verified-as-fixed bugs still get a real repro check before the Closed\n  transition is proposed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab3937e88019a1189cffdb5f7af90219e1f3c7c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/ab3937e88019a1189cffdb5f7af90219e1f3c7c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDg4ZWM4OTkwOTY3YmUxMzlmZTFjMGVlNzE1ZDdmMTJjODA0OWNlNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e","sha":"249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e"}],"sha":"88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/88ec8990967be139fe1c0ee715d7f12c8049ce6b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T15:22:40Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T15:22:40Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"Add v6.0: bug-bash workflow (agent + command) and README update\n\n- bug-bash-runner agent: two-phase batched bug triage + per-ticket TDD fix\n  loop with mandatory verify -> pause -> fix checkpoint, subagent fan-out\n  at every parallelizable phase, and memory-driven project knobs\n- /bug-bash slash command: kicks off the agent in triage-only mode against\n  a list of Jira keys or an umbrella in a multi-repo CWD\n- README: agent #15 entry, commands-table row, when-to-use rows, v6.0\n  version history bullet\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e31ee320072f9831630833f4f4b0df5a100ffe22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/trees/e31ee320072f9831630833f4f4b0df5a100ffe22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/git/commits/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e","node_id":"C_kwDOQXsyI9oAKDI0OWE3M2U2ZDk1YmZiMTRjODQ1ODkzNzU1YWU4MWJiMjFhODRiMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commit/2f0848232a1919a7162f9bcbe77a75098467b48d","sha":"2f0848232a1919a7162f9bcbe77a75098467b48d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/2f0848232a1919a7162f9bcbe77a75098467b48d"}],"sha":"249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/249a73e6d95bfb14c845893755ae81bb21a84b1e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scottyj503/ai-prompts/commits/2f0848232a1919a7162f9bcbe77a75098467b48d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T19:23:54Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T19:23:54Z","email":"scottjones@Scott-Jones---0267---MacBook-Pro-14.local","name":"Scott Jones"},"message":"Update review command: explicit opus model per agent, dynamic ADR discovery\n\n- Add explicit subagent_type and model: opus to each of the five agent tasks\n- Replace hardcoded ADR-0