_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/01915599f71c1f931f984d922b60d1ad6d9d41c1","node_id":"C_kwDOQZGHK9oAKDAxOTE1NTk5ZjcxYzFmOTMxZjk4NGQ5MjJiNjBkMWFkNmQ5ZDQxYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94","sha":"845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/89cff0c5c9d94e79e4da89f6027cd62bb80c1413","sha":"89cff0c5c9d94e79e4da89f6027cd62bb80c1413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/89cff0c5c9d94e79e4da89f6027cd62bb80c1413"}],"sha":"01915599f71c1f931f984d922b60d1ad6d9d41c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/01915599f71c1f931f984d922b60d1ad6d9d41c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169318143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/OlivieriD","id":169318143,"login":"OlivieriD","node_id":"U_kgDOCheW_w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:53:49Z","email":"olivedufort@gmail.com","name":"OlivierD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:53:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump axios from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2 (#213)\n\nBumps [axios](https://github.com/axios/axios) from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/releases\">axios''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<h2>v1.15.1</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation\nand sanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>Location</code> Request Header Type:</strong> Adds\n<code>Location</code> to <code>CommonRequestHeadersList</code> for\naccurate typing of redirect-aware requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7528\">#7528</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FormData Handling:</strong> Removes\n<code>Content-Type</code> when no boundary is present on\n<code>FormData</code> fetch requests, supports multi-select fields,\ncancels <code>request.body</code> instead of the source stream on fetch\nabort, and fixes a recursion bug in form-data serialisation. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7314\">#7314</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10676\">#10676</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10702\">#10702</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10726\">#10726</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP Adapter:</strong> Handles socket-only request errors\nwithout leaking keep-alive listeners. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10576\">#10576</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Progress Events:</strong> Clamps <code>loaded</code> to\n<code>total</code> for computable upload/download progress events.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7458\">#7458</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Types:</strong> Aligns <code>runWhen</code> type with the\nruntime behaviour in <code>InterceptorManager</code> and makes response\nheader keys case-insensitive. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7529\">#7529</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10677\">#10677</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>buildFullPath</code>:</strong> Uses strict equality in\nthe base/relative URL check. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7252\">#7252</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>AxiosURLSearchParams</code> Regex:</strong> Improves\nthe regex used for param serialisation to avoid edge-case mismatches.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10736\">#10736</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Resilient Value Parsing:</strong> Parses out header/config\nvalues instead of throwing on malformed input. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10687\">#10687</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/v1.x/CHANGELOG.md\">axios''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2 - April 21, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>v1.15.1 - April 19, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation and\nsanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/582934382e4e0e0bcb679c628071a4203e93cf57\"><code>5829343</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10789\">#10789</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/4709a48fa2717ba97f43f5432d48ca4e26c2d326\"><code>4709a48</code></a>\nfix: added fix for memory leak in sockets (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/be3336014e01f9a4fc1f8aef15303cf7daaf58db\"><code>be33360</code></a>\nchore: update changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/47915144662f2733e6c051bdcb895a8c8f0586aa\"><code>4791514</code></a>\nfix: more header pollutions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/6feafcff6c2dbafe206161c5d09e38e1d36af66f\"><code>6feafcf</code></a>\nfix: socket issue (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/302e2739c602f00e323d4f3f5c79500647633a73\"><code>302e273</code></a>\ndocs: update docs, add a couple actions etc (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/ac42446be51300fe214ba3c6e40cc95f34fd6871\"><code>ac42446</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10767\">#10767</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/908f2206b6bfeff67236784abce85935698ac1d9\"><code>908f220</code></a>\ndocs: update threatmodel (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10765\">#10765</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/f93f8155250c2e066205521eda05ae22983a1f6d\"><code>f93f815</code></a>\ndocs: added docs around potential decompressions bomb (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10763\">#10763</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/1728aa1b15b8857f970611fd8983c06b423fc486\"><code>1728aa1</code></a>\nfix: short-circuits on any truthy non-boolean in withXSRFToken (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.13.5...v1.15.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Install script changes</summary>\n<p>This version modifies <code>prepare</code> script that runs during\ninstallation. Review the package contents before updating.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=axios&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=1.13.5&new-version=1.15.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/network/alerts).\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"e992aa8c2b5613a9d9a5e9d4724694196a257e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/git/trees/e992aa8c2b5613a9d9a5e9d4724694196a257e4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/git/commits/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94","verification":{"payload":"tree e992aa8c2b5613a9d9a5e9d4724694196a257e4b\nparent 4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf\nparent 087bb6cc6464d83196376d8327bf6b3973e90e21\nauthor OlivierD <olivedufort@gmail.com> 1778540029 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778540029 -0400\n\nBump axios from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2 (#213)\n\nBumps [axios](https://github.com/axios/axios) from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/releases\">axios''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<h2>v1.15.1</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation\nand sanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>Location</code> Request Header Type:</strong> Adds\n<code>Location</code> to <code>CommonRequestHeadersList</code> for\naccurate typing of redirect-aware requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7528\">#7528</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FormData Handling:</strong> Removes\n<code>Content-Type</code> when no boundary is present on\n<code>FormData</code> fetch requests, supports multi-select fields,\ncancels <code>request.body</code> instead of the source stream on fetch\nabort, and fixes a recursion bug in form-data serialisation. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7314\">#7314</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10676\">#10676</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10702\">#10702</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10726\">#10726</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP Adapter:</strong> Handles socket-only request errors\nwithout leaking keep-alive listeners. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10576\">#10576</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Progress Events:</strong> Clamps <code>loaded</code> to\n<code>total</code> for computable upload/download progress events.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7458\">#7458</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Types:</strong> Aligns <code>runWhen</code> type with the\nruntime behaviour in <code>InterceptorManager</code> and makes response\nheader keys case-insensitive. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7529\">#7529</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10677\">#10677</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>buildFullPath</code>:</strong> Uses strict equality in\nthe base/relative URL check. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7252\">#7252</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>AxiosURLSearchParams</code> Regex:</strong> Improves\nthe regex used for param serialisation to avoid edge-case mismatches.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10736\">#10736</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Resilient Value Parsing:</strong> Parses out header/config\nvalues instead of throwing on malformed input. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10687\">#10687</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/v1.x/CHANGELOG.md\">axios''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2 - April 21, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>v1.15.1 - April 19, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation and\nsanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/582934382e4e0e0bcb679c628071a4203e93cf57\"><code>5829343</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10789\">#10789</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/4709a48fa2717ba97f43f5432d48ca4e26c2d326\"><code>4709a48</code></a>\nfix: added fix for memory leak in sockets (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/be3336014e01f9a4fc1f8aef15303cf7daaf58db\"><code>be33360</code></a>\nchore: update changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/47915144662f2733e6c051bdcb895a8c8f0586aa\"><code>4791514</code></a>\nfix: more header pollutions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/6feafcff6c2dbafe206161c5d09e38e1d36af66f\"><code>6feafcf</code></a>\nfix: socket issue (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/302e2739c602f00e323d4f3f5c79500647633a73\"><code>302e273</code></a>\ndocs: update docs, add a couple actions etc (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/ac42446be51300fe214ba3c6e40cc95f34fd6871\"><code>ac42446</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10767\">#10767</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/908f2206b6bfeff67236784abce85935698ac1d9\"><code>908f220</code></a>\ndocs: update threatmodel (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10765\">#10765</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/f93f8155250c2e066205521eda05ae22983a1f6d\"><code>f93f815</code></a>\ndocs: added docs around potential decompressions bomb (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10763\">#10763</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/1728aa1b15b8857f970611fd8983c06b423fc486\"><code>1728aa1</code></a>\nfix: short-circuits on any truthy non-boolean in withXSRFToken (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.13.5...v1.15.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Install script changes</summary>\n<p>This version modifies <code>prepare</code> script that runs during\ninstallation. Review the package contents before updating.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=axios&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=1.13.5&new-version=1.15.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/network/alerts).\n\n</details>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAl39CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATz0QAIcKbH/y6Bq5f+EZxU6tZrDs\njUZkjHFTyVTPuIJ9jBnH+g6nnlydeio1jER+71kh8edYxwvzzsaQ3S/3vdk+ZE+r\nje0THMTYrb3pgGFzL+2GrTF5CVu/p7Ksk9CBiopX/atB0Kshzv+pHDyRyCqM2c+4\nCLY88XSmmb3ZZdoAJ/nui3DbF95rC4SPnZnNQCV9vceUmhyhSLUnZhbHiiSqGlJ+\n+RTIcy4Al3MDemXSOeKQcufd9HU+BI3y4wp47iAyjQuHhZa+kzzyxf8bB3imXqiy\no4xPvYAnWT4xJ5oxcfIY2FMJO4rD47Kn9UHWlBLjoMwPfAhdh1no0c4Hhlk+NrPJ\nTkaPhpoijbayEHqP4AanJksBA3OmSoHBjogMAteKi9iueAnfhnyOyngjDi6iqIQd\nhsZHb6pSI2a5QT0M/nzo77rpbULqWWTs4w/QPib45bp5lz4zD78+GHOZRp/ofOWl\nqZMinh4/+XFErDaF9cR2L6/zqiwQ9L7HJKYwuj7aSoScqgovjNUJZBcGrGXijLbN\n1vB/Yo3MrslyIheySCybSK3N0kaoLglc8Aryew2pdKiHu3nANq7eaODVURa9WHCF\nd+xyDeivcL2MX4R27roF4WmdBKB/8xjg4185vD0xapaSAEEHy0LcG6TGaoBAT97F\ndm5sRYLqcdeAu1jIUT8k\n=lxJW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T22:53:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94","node_id":"C_kwDOQZGHK9oAKDg0NWQ2ODlkNmE2ZjhjNDYwNTE4OGVkMDgwYjM4YmQ3YTdjODllOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf","sha":"4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commit/087bb6cc6464d83196376d8327bf6b3973e90e21","sha":"087bb6cc6464d83196376d8327bf6b3973e90e21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/087bb6cc6464d83196376d8327bf6b3973e90e21"}],"sha":"845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/845d689d6a6f8c4605188ed080b38bd7a7c89e94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169318143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/OlivieriD","id":169318143,"login":"OlivieriD","node_id":"U_kgDOCheW_w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlivieriD","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/commits/4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:53:15Z","email":"olivedufort@gmail.com","name":"OlivierD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:53:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump axios from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2 in /frontend/les_constructions_dominic_cyr (#212)\n\nBumps [axios](https://github.com/axios/axios) from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/releases\">axios''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<h2>v1.15.1</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation\nand sanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>Location</code> Request Header Type:</strong> Adds\n<code>Location</code> to <code>CommonRequestHeadersList</code> for\naccurate typing of redirect-aware requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7528\">#7528</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FormData Handling:</strong> Removes\n<code>Content-Type</code> when no boundary is present on\n<code>FormData</code> fetch requests, supports multi-select fields,\ncancels <code>request.body</code> instead of the source stream on fetch\nabort, and fixes a recursion bug in form-data serialisation. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7314\">#7314</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10676\">#10676</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10702\">#10702</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10726\">#10726</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP Adapter:</strong> Handles socket-only request errors\nwithout leaking keep-alive listeners. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10576\">#10576</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Progress Events:</strong> Clamps <code>loaded</code> to\n<code>total</code> for computable upload/download progress events.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7458\">#7458</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Types:</strong> Aligns <code>runWhen</code> type with the\nruntime behaviour in <code>InterceptorManager</code> and makes response\nheader keys case-insensitive. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7529\">#7529</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10677\">#10677</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>buildFullPath</code>:</strong> Uses strict equality in\nthe base/relative URL check. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7252\">#7252</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>AxiosURLSearchParams</code> Regex:</strong> Improves\nthe regex used for param serialisation to avoid edge-case mismatches.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10736\">#10736</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Resilient Value Parsing:</strong> Parses out header/config\nvalues instead of throwing on malformed input. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10687\">#10687</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/v1.x/CHANGELOG.md\">axios''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2 - April 21, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>v1.15.1 - April 19, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation and\nsanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/582934382e4e0e0bcb679c628071a4203e93cf57\"><code>5829343</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10789\">#10789</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/4709a48fa2717ba97f43f5432d48ca4e26c2d326\"><code>4709a48</code></a>\nfix: added fix for memory leak in sockets (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/be3336014e01f9a4fc1f8aef15303cf7daaf58db\"><code>be33360</code></a>\nchore: update changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/47915144662f2733e6c051bdcb895a8c8f0586aa\"><code>4791514</code></a>\nfix: more header pollutions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/6feafcff6c2dbafe206161c5d09e38e1d36af66f\"><code>6feafcf</code></a>\nfix: socket issue (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/302e2739c602f00e323d4f3f5c79500647633a73\"><code>302e273</code></a>\ndocs: update docs, add a couple actions etc (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/ac42446be51300fe214ba3c6e40cc95f34fd6871\"><code>ac42446</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10767\">#10767</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/908f2206b6bfeff67236784abce85935698ac1d9\"><code>908f220</code></a>\ndocs: update threatmodel (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10765\">#10765</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/f93f8155250c2e066205521eda05ae22983a1f6d\"><code>f93f815</code></a>\ndocs: added docs around potential decompressions bomb (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10763\">#10763</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/1728aa1b15b8857f970611fd8983c06b423fc486\"><code>1728aa1</code></a>\nfix: short-circuits on any truthy non-boolean in withXSRFToken (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.13.5...v1.15.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Install script changes</summary>\n<p>This version modifies <code>prepare</code> script that runs during\ninstallation. Review the package contents before updating.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=axios&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=1.13.5&new-version=1.15.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/network/alerts).\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"c4036a06143714e58f89473263483012cc67a08e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/git/trees/c4036a06143714e58f89473263483012cc67a08e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LCDCI/Les-Constructions-Dominic-Cyr/git/commits/4b910233615a7dbb0746baa363033d91cce2c1cf","verification":{"payload":"tree c4036a06143714e58f89473263483012cc67a08e\nparent dc5b219cd8b84bfcf30f6992c47fda20b5589310\nparent eb84c29479c4d2e0be4834aa656b7379580a226a\nauthor OlivierD <olivedufort@gmail.com> 1778539995 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778539995 -0400\n\nBump axios from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2 in /frontend/les_constructions_dominic_cyr (#212)\n\nBumps [axios](https://github.com/axios/axios) from 1.13.5 to 1.15.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/releases\">axios''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<h2>v1.15.1</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation\nand sanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>Location</code> Request Header Type:</strong> Adds\n<code>Location</code> to <code>CommonRequestHeadersList</code> for\naccurate typing of redirect-aware requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7528\">#7528</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FormData Handling:</strong> Removes\n<code>Content-Type</code> when no boundary is present on\n<code>FormData</code> fetch requests, supports multi-select fields,\ncancels <code>request.body</code> instead of the source stream on fetch\nabort, and fixes a recursion bug in form-data serialisation. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7314\">#7314</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10676\">#10676</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10702\">#10702</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10726\">#10726</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP Adapter:</strong> Handles socket-only request errors\nwithout leaking keep-alive listeners. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10576\">#10576</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Progress Events:</strong> Clamps <code>loaded</code> to\n<code>total</code> for computable upload/download progress events.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7458\">#7458</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Types:</strong> Aligns <code>runWhen</code> type with the\nruntime behaviour in <code>InterceptorManager</code> and makes response\nheader keys case-insensitive. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7529\">#7529</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10677\">#10677</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>buildFullPath</code>:</strong> Uses strict equality in\nthe base/relative URL check. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/7252\">#7252</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>AxiosURLSearchParams</code> Regex:</strong> Improves\nthe regex used for param serialisation to avoid edge-case mismatches.\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10736\">#10736</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Resilient Value Parsing:</strong> Parses out header/config\nvalues instead of throwing on malformed input. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10687\">#10687</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/v1.x/CHANGELOG.md\">axios''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.15.2 - April 21, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release delivers prototype-pollution hardening for the Node HTTP\nadapter, adds an opt-in <code>allowedSocketPaths</code> allowlist to\nmitigate SSRF via Unix domain sockets, fixes a keep-alive socket memory\nleak, and ships supply-chain hardening across CI and security docs.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prototype Pollution Hardening (HTTP Adapter):</strong>\nHardened the Node HTTP adapter and\n<code>resolveConfig</code>/<code>mergeConfig</code>/validator paths to\nread only own properties and use null-prototype config objects,\npreventing polluted <code>auth</code>, <code>baseURL</code>,\n<code>socketPath</code>, <code>beforeRedirect</code>, and\n<code>insecureHTTPParser</code> from influencing requests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>SSRF via <code>socketPath</code>:</strong> Rejects\nnon-string <code>socketPath</code> values and adds an opt-in\n<code>allowedSocketPaths</code> config option to restrict permitted Unix\ndomain socket paths, returning <code>AxiosError</code>\n<code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code> on mismatch. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n<li><strong>Supply-chain Hardening:</strong> Added <code>.npmrc</code>\nwith <code>ignore-scripts=true</code>, lockfile lint CI, non-blocking\nreproducible build diff, scoped CODEOWNERS, expanded\n<code>SECURITY.md</code>/<code>THREATMODEL.md</code> with provenance\nverification (<code>npm audit signatures</code>), 60-day resolution\npolicy, and maintainer incident-response runbook. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>allowedSocketPaths</code> Config Option:</strong> New\nrequest config option (and TypeScript types) to allowlist Unix domain\nsocket paths used by the Node http adapter; backwards compatible when\nunset. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep-alive Socket Memory Leak:</strong> Installs a single\nper-socket <code>error</code> listener tracking the active request via\n<code>kAxiosSocketListener</code>/<code>kAxiosCurrentReq</code>,\neliminating per-request listener accumulation,\n<code>MaxListenersExceededWarning</code>, and linear heap growth under\nconcurrent or long-running keep-alive workloads (fixes <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10780\">#10780</a>).\n(<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changelog:</strong> Updated <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> with\nv1.15.1 release notes. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.15.1...v1.15.2\">Full\nChangelog</a></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>v1.15.1 - April 19, 2026</h2>\n<p>This release ships a coordinated set of security hardening fixes\nacross headers, body/redirect limits, multipart handling, and\nXSRF/prototype-pollution vectors, alongside a broad sweep of bug fixes,\ntest migrations, and threat-model documentation updates.</p>\n<h2>🔒 Security Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Header Injection Hardening:</strong> Tightened validation and\nsanitisation across request header construction to close the\nheader-injection attack surface. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10749\">#10749</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>CRLF Stripping in Multipart Headers:</strong> Correctly\nstrips CR/LF from multipart header values to prevent injection via field\nnames and filenames. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10758\">#10758</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Prototype Pollution / Auth Bypass:</strong> Replaced unsafe\n<code>in</code> checks with <code>hasOwnProperty</code> to prevent\nauthentication bypass via prototype pollution on config objects, with\nadditional regression tests. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10761\">#10761</a></strong>,\n<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10760\">#10760</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>withXSRFToken</code> Truthy Bypass:</strong>\nShort-circuits on any truthy non-boolean value, so an ambiguous config\nno longer silently leaks the XSRF token cross-origin. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>maxBodyLength</code> With Zero Redirects:</strong>\nEnforces <code>maxBodyLength</code> even when <code>maxRedirects</code>\nis set to <code>0</code>, closing a bypass path for oversized request\nbodies. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10753\">#10753</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Streamed Response <code>maxContentLength</code>\nBypass:</strong> Applies <code>maxContentLength</code> to streamed\nresponses that previously bypassed the cap. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10754\">#10754</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Follow-up CVE Completion:</strong> Completes an earlier\nincomplete CVE fix to fully close the regression window. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10755\">#10755</a></strong>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🚀 New Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI-Based Docs Translations:</strong> Initial scaffold for\nAI-assisted translations of the documentation site. (<strong><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10705\">#10705</a></strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/582934382e4e0e0bcb679c628071a4203e93cf57\"><code>5829343</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10789\">#10789</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/4709a48fa2717ba97f43f5432d48ca4e26c2d326\"><code>4709a48</code></a>\nfix: added fix for memory leak in sockets (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10788\">#10788</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/be3336014e01f9a4fc1f8aef15303cf7daaf58db\"><code>be33360</code></a>\nchore: update changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10781\">#10781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/47915144662f2733e6c051bdcb895a8c8f0586aa\"><code>4791514</code></a>\nfix: more header pollutions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10779\">#10779</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/6feafcff6c2dbafe206161c5d09e38e1d36af66f\"><code>6feafcf</code></a>\nfix: socket issue (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10777\">#10777</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/302e2739c602f00e323d4f3f5c79500647633a73\"><code>302e273</code></a>\ndocs: update docs, add a couple actions etc (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10776\">#10776</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/ac42446be51300fe214ba3c6e40cc95f34fd6871\"><code>ac42446</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare release 1.15.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10767\">#10767</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/908f2206b6bfeff67236784abce85935698ac1d9\"><code>908f220</code></a>\ndocs: update threatmodel (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10765\">#10765</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/f93f8155250c2e066205521eda05ae22983a1f6d\"><code>f93f815</code></a>\ndocs: added docs around potential decompressions bomb (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10763\">#10763</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/1728aa1b15b8857f970611fd8983c06b423fc486\"><code>1728aa1</code></a>\nfix: short-circuits on any truthy non-boolean in withXSRFToken (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/issues/10762\">#10762</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/compare/v1.13.5...v1.15.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Install script changes</summary>\n<p>This version modifies <code>prepare</code> script that runs during\ninstallation. Review the package contents before updating.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n